Titre$Dacrymyces_McNabb
Com$Adapt Gf mai 2013
1,40$ TAXONOMY
1,42 $ SOURCE
1,45$REFERENCES
1,2 $ Basidiocarps variable in shape, pustulate, pulvinate, applanate, or  complicate, sessile or stipitate with a flabellate, spathulate or  convoluted pileus; hymenium amphigenous, well defined cortex  absent, thin- or thick-walled hairs occasionally present on base  of basidiocarp or stipe .. 2. $$s"subgenus Dacrymyces"
bug corrigé
1,25 $ Basidiocarps turbinate, pezizoid, or cupulate, sessile to stipitate;  hymenium confined to surface of dise or interior of cup; well  defined cortex present, composed of a palisade of thin- or  thick-walled, septate hairs 26. $$s"subgenus Turbinaster"
2,3 $ Clamp connections present
2,12 $ Clamp connections absent
3,0 $ Basidiospores subglobose to broadly ovate, muriform  $ D. ovisporus  1.
3,4 $ Basidiospores cylindrical, curved-cylindrical or allantoid
4,0 $ Basidiospores 3-7-septate; dikaryophyses simple or sparingly branched  apically, with clamp connections throughout their length   $ D. nigrescens  2.
4,5 $ Basidiospores 0-3-septate
5,6 $ Dikaryophyses consistently finely and irregularly branched apically
5,8 $ Dikaryophyses simple, cylindrical, occasionally sparingly branched
6,0 $ Basidiospores thin-walled with thin septa, 1-3-septate  $ D. enatus var. enatus 3.
6,7 $ Basidiospores thick-walled with thickened septa, 3-septate
7,0 $ Basidiocarps drying dark brown to dull black, 3-4 mm diam.; basidiospores  11-15.5 x 4.5-6.5 µm $ D. enatus var. macrosporus 4.
7,0 $ Basidiocarps drying reddish brown to dark brownish black, less than  3 mm diam.; basidiospores 13.5-21 x 5-7 µm $ D. paraphysatus 5.
8,9 $ Basidiocarps applanate, effused, often coalescing to form irregular masses
8,10 $ Basidiocarps pustulate or pulvinate, rarely coalescing
9,0 $ Basidiocarps pallid amber to brown when fresh, drying dark brown to  black; basidiospores 11-17.5 X 5-6.5 µm, 3-septate $ D. adpressus 6.
9,0 $ Basidiocarps pallid yellow or yellow-buff when fresh, drying dull  brown, reddish brown or rust coloured; basidiospores 13-18 x  4 7 µm. 1-3-septate $ D. corticioides 7.
10,0 $ Basidiocarps large, to 15 x 4 mm, cerebriform, pallid amber, amberclay  or faintly smoky amber when fresh $ D. cokeri 8.
10,11 $ Basidiocarps small, rarely more than 2.5 mm diam
11,0 $ Basidiospores 8-15 X 3.5-5 µm, tardily 1-3-septate $ D. tortus  9.
11,0 $ Basidiospores 14-23 X 5-6.5 µm. 3-septate  $ D. confluera 10.
12,13 $ Basidiospores I -3-septate
12,20 $ Basidiospores at least 7-septate
13,0 $ Basidiospores constantly 1-septate, 8-12 X 3-4 µm; basidiocarps  turbinate or stipitate with an undulate-discoid or semi-flabellate  pileus $ D. microsporus  11.
13,14 $ Basidiospores 1-3-septate
14,0 $ Basidiocarps large, 4-18 mm diam., to 20 mm high, stoutly stipitate;  pileus hemispherical, irregularly flabellate or spathulate; basidiospores  10.5-15.5 x 3.3-4.5 µm, 3-septate, septa thickened $ D. dacryomitriformis  12.
14,15 $ Basidiocarps small, rarely more than 6 mm diam., less in height,  sessile or short-stipitate
15,16 $ Basidiospores distinctly thick-walled, septa thickened
15,17 $ Basidiospores thin-walled, septa thin
16,0 $ Basidiocarps minute, 0.2-1 mm diam.; probasidia stoutly cylindricalsubclavate;  thick-walled hairs present at base of basidiocarp $ D. intermedius  13.
16,0 $ Basidiocarps 1-4 mm diam.; probasidia slender; arthrospores often  present in separate fructifications or occasionally mixed with  basidia $ D. stillatus 14.
17,18 $ Basidiocarps sessile
17,19 $ Basidiocarps stipitate, turbinate or piston-shaped
18,0 $ Basidiocarps irregularly pezizoid, gyrose or lobed, thin, 1-3 mm diam.  $ D. lacrymalis 15.
18,0 $ Basidiocarps pustulate or pulvinate, 0.5-2 mm diam $ D. minor 16.
19,0 $ Basidiocarps often short-stipitate, attached by a whitish radicating  base, cerebriform; basidiospores 11-17 x 3.5-7 µm, 3-septate  $ D. capitatus  17.
19,0 $ Basidiocarps turbinate or piston-shaped; basidiospores 9-13.5 x  3.5-4.5 µm. l-(3)-septate $ D. cupularis 18.
20,0 $ Basidiospores muriform, thick-walled with thickened septa, broadly  and bluntly fusiform, occasionally subglobose to ovate, 22.5-30  x 9-13.5 µm $ D. dictyosporus 19.
20,21 $ Basidiospores not muriform
21,0 $ Probasidia basally inflated, obclavate; basidiospores strongly allantoid,  20-28.5 x 5.5-7.7 µm. 15 or more septate $ D. falcatus 20.
21,22 $ Probasidia not basally inflated, cylindrical-subclavate
22,0 $ Apically branched dikaryophyses present; basidiospores curvedcylindrical,  15.5-23.6 x 4.7-6.8 µm, 7-12-septate $ D. san-augustinii  21.
22,23 $ Apically branched dikaryophyses absent
23,0 $ Basidiospores inflated-cylindrical, 15-24 x 6-9.5 µm, 7-septate;  basidiocarps stipitate and pileate $ D. coryneoides 22.
23,24 $ Basidiospores curved-cylindrical to allantoid
24,0 $ Basidiocarps applanate; basidiospores 7-(9)-septate, septa thin,  indistinct $ D. novae-zelandiac 23.
24,0 $ Basidiocarps extremely variable in shape, pulvinate, flabellate, stipitate  with a spathulate, cupulate, convoluted or patellate pileus, often  forming cerebriform or complicate masses; basidiospores  7-septate, septa thickened, distinct $ D. chrysospermus 24.
25,26 $ Clamp connections présent
25,0 $ Clamp connections absent; probasidia obclavate or urniform; basidiospores  oblong-elliptical to broadly elliptical, 17.5-26.5 x  9-12 µm $ D. estonicus 25.
26,0 $ Basidiospores 3-septate, 13-19.5 x 4.5-6 µm . $ D. minutus 26.
26,27 $ Basidiospores more than 3-septate, at least predominantly so
27,0 $ Basidiocarps large, to 10 mm diam., sessile, margins conspicuous,  involute; basidiospores 16.5-27.5 x 5.5-8.5 µm, 7-(l l)-septate  $ D. margimitus 27.
27,28 $ Basidiocarps small, rarely to 6 mm diam., sessile, turbinate or shortstipitate
28,0 $ Basidiocarps turbinate, to 6 mm high; basidiospores thin-walled,  18.5-26.5 x 6.5-11 µm, 7-septate $ D. pedunculatus 28.
28,29 $ Basidiocarps cupulate, pezizoid or pulvinate and centrally depressed
29,0 $ Basidiospores consistently thick-walled with thickened septa, often  muriform, 24-32 x 7.5-11 µm, transversely 7-septate, frequently  with 1-3-(5) longitudinal septa $ D. chrysocomus 29.
29,30 $ Basidiospores typically thin-walled, occasionally thick-walled with  irregularly thickened septa, rarely muriform
30,0 $ Basidiocarps cupulate, substipitate or stipitate; basidiospores 15.5-26  x 5 7 µm, 7-septate $ D. suédois 30.
30,0 $ Basidiocarps pulvinate and centrally depressed, sessile; basidiospores  12-30.5 x 6-9.5 µm, 3-7-septate, rarely with 1-2 longitudinal  septa $ D. variisporus 31.
40,0$ Dacrymyces Nees ex Fries, Syst. mycol. 1: lv. 1821.///Arrhytidia Berk. & Curt. in Berk., Hook. J. Bot. & Kew Gdn Mise. 1: 235. 1849.///Septocolla Bon., Handbk. Allg. Mykol. 152. 1851.///Fructifications extremely variable in size and shape, originating as  pustules, becoming pulvinate, discoid, turbinate or pezizoid, often  stipitate with a spathulate, flabellate, discoid, pezizoid, subglobose,  lobed or cerebriform pileus, remaining discrète or coalescing to form  irregular masses, sometimes efïused and applanate but always retaining  evidence of pustular origin, usually attached to substratum by a point  or rooting base, very occasionally broadly attached. Consistency softgelatinous  to firm-gelatinous. Composition homogeneous exclusive of  cortical hairs and cells, composed of thin-walled hyphae variously gelatinised,  clamp connections present or absent. Cortex present or absent,  when present composed of a palisade of thin- or thick-walled, septate  hairs, terminal cells cylindrical, subclavate, oate, or occasionally obpyriform.///Hymenium amphigenous or confined to superior surface in species  with a cortex, composed of basidia, dikaryophyses present or absent;  probasidia cylindrical-subclavate, occasionally obclavate or urniform;  metabasidia bisterigmate. Basidiospores cylindrical, curved-cylindrical,  allantoid, occasionally broadly and bluntly fusiform, ovate, or subglobose,  apiculate, septate at maturity. Germination by conidia and/or  germ tubes.///TYPE SPECIES: Dacrymyces stillatus Nees ex Fr.

 42,0$Taxonomic Studies in the Dacrymycetaceae///VIII. Dacrymyces Nees ex Fries ///R. F. R . MCNABB* Botany Department, University of Canterbury, Christchurch /// (New Zealand Journal of Botany 11: 461-524. Received 18 May 1973)

